35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Nine complaints died out because no one was responsible. The neighbouring block’s charge made two people stop attending meetings. We need a system that doesn’t isolate people.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, the minutes confirm the grumbling! The same flats held the covered spots for five years with zero review. It’s definitely not just noise.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, that confirms the stagnation. My data shows four of eleven morning departures required shifting another bike. The rain exposure is also severe past the downpipe.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, shifting bikes is a symptom, not the cause. The ledger shows zero capital funds, so any fix needs a levy. The station park costs 2,600 yen monthly.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The frame trial showed twenty seconds per lift, and the treasurer logs three hours monthly just for current collections. Adding per-place billing would double that burden.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, three hours monthly is unsustainable. If we add billing, we risk repeating the neighbouring block’s isolation. We need a system that doesn’t demand constant enforcement.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that’s a lot of work! But the daily riders said they’d rather pay than be treated equally. Maybe a small fee is worth it?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, willingness to pay doesn’t solve the physical bottleneck. Four shifts per morning is a structural failure. We need to address the layout, not just the money.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, “rather pay” is a sentiment, not a budget. The ledger is empty. If we charge, we’re levying everyone for a service only some use. That’s a different conversation.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the ledger is empty, but the workload is the real trap. Three hours monthly is already a burden; adding billing guarantees it lapses.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, I agree. The neighbouring block proves that financial friction isolates people. We need a solution that minimizes administrative burden and prevents social fracture.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! But the minutes prove the current setup is unfair. We need a change that’s actually doable, not just a new headache for the treasurer.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, fairness is secondary to function. My data shows the layout forces physical conflict. We must fix the bottleneck before debating fees.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, you’re ignoring the money. The station park charges 2,600 yen. If we don’t price this, we’re subsidizing it with empty pockets. That’s not a solution.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the bottleneck is real, but the maintenance is the killer. If the spring needs greasing twice a year, who does it? I won’t be the one.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the layout is broken, but @Toshio, the maintenance burden is the real trap. We need a system that doesn’t collapse under its own weight.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I hear you! But if we just open the racks, won’t the same people grab the dry spots again? I want fairness, not just speed!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, open racks eliminate the shifting bottleneck. The rain is a separate issue. We fix the flow first, then address the weather.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, fairness is cheap if it breaks the budget. The ledger is empty. If we don’t price it, we’re subsidizing it with nothing. That’s not a solution.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, open racks mean no billing, but the greasing remains. If nobody owns the maintenance, it dies. I need a system that doesn’t rely on my goodwill.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
